<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico to drain 7.386 bln pesos.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico to drain 7.386 bln pesos.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico sought to drain 7.386 billion pesos from the secondary market on Tuesday through a combination of three direct sales of paper and eight repurchase agreements, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were offered or assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT	 TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>	150 million    352 days   22.89 pct</p>
<p>	150 million    177 days   21.69 pct</p>
<p>	150 million     86 days</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were offered as follows:</p>
<p>    1.000 bln     44 days</p>
<p>    1.000 bln     41 days</p>
<p>    1.000 bln     36 days</p>
<p>    1.000 bln     31 days</p>
<p>    1.000 bln     16 days</p>
<p>	700 million	9 days</p>
<p>    1.000 bln	2 days</p>
<p>	236 million	1 day</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
